# Index Cannon
Authority: Tier2 operational checklist
Updated: 2026-06-17

Tier1 source: `docs/fireux-canon.md`

## Purpose
Keep index pages boring, comparable, and easy to align across entity families.

An index page lists a family. It is not the console, not a dev probe, not a bespoke landing page, and not a place to hide fetching policy.

## Family Matrix

| Family | Job | Current examples | Same As Other Indexes | Allowed Difference |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Console-backed public root | Browse root records that can also be operated in a console | `/kitchens`, `/suppliers`, `/portfolios`, `/properties`, `/projects` | `UPage`, `UPageHeader`, `UPageBody`, `EntityIndexCta`, one `XCollectionManager` | CTA points toward console/operator flow; collection manager owns fetching and filtering |
| System root directory | Browse FireUX system entities | `/apps`, `/ecosystems`, `/modules` | public page shell, CTA, collection manager | may split featured/all sections only when documented; may use system app settings |
| Public domain directory | Browse ordinary public root/profile records | `/places`, `/companies`, `/products`, `/blog`, `/jobs`, `/chefs`, `/professionals`, `/agents`, `/users`, `/ingredients` | public page shell plus one domain CTA/collection manager | older pages may still pass collections; target state is manager-owned collection behavior |
| Public doorway/onboarding | Create a stable public doorway before the entity is fully integrated | `/menus` | public page shell, CTA, one primary tool/action, one collection manager | may include an upload/tool card before the manager; record may later bridge into a scoped entity |
| Scoped public child index | List public children under a selected parent/scope | `/kitchens/[slug]/menus` | page shell and public unavailable state | must resolve exact parent scope first; no first/default/active parent fallback |
| Detail root index | Render one record at a folder root so child routes can exist | `/menus/[menuId]/index.vue`, `/kitchens/[slug]/index.vue`, `/companies/[id]/index.vue` | header/body/profile/operator rhythm where applicable | not a collection index; may fetch one exact record and expose child routes such as `/qr` or `/upgrade` |
| Console target index | Choose or inspect the selected console target | `/console/kitchen`, `/console/supplier`, `/console/portfolio`, `/console/property`, `/console/project`, `/console/blank` | dashboard panel, console navbar, `ConsoleXIndex` component | not public `UPage`; requires auth; selection logic lives in console spine |
| Console operation index | Manage child records for a selected console target | `/console/kitchen/menus`, `/console/kitchen/dishes`, `/console/kitchen/recipes`, `/console/kitchen/ingredients` | dashboard panel, console navbar, operation component | requires selected target; operation reads selected runtime, not route guesses |
| Admin management index | Private/admin CRUD for app or package maintainers | `/admin/products`, `/admin/blogs`, `/admin/licenses` | may use header/body/collection manager | not public browse; must be auth/admin gated and may skip public CTA |
| App/product landing index | Product home, pricing, docs, dev, onboarding, solution landing | `/`, `/pricing`, `/solutions`, `/dev`, `/docs/**`, `/onboarding` | no entity-index requirement | not an entity index; may be bespoke marketing/docs UI |

## Similarity Rule
- Public entity indexes should look comparable from the outside: header, short description, one CTA or growth prompt, and the family collection surface.
- Console indexes should look comparable to other console indexes, not to public indexes.
- Operation indexes should look comparable to other operation indexes inside the same console family.
- Detail root indexes should be compared with other detail roots, not collection indexes.

## Difference Rule
- Differences must come from the family job, not from local convenience.
- A page may differ because it is root, scoped, doorway, console, operation, admin, or landing.
- A page should not differ because it locally fetched, locally filtered, invented a CTA shape, or bypassed the family collection manager.

## Canon Shape
Every public/runtime entity index should start from this spine:

```vue
<template>
  <UPage>
    <UPageHeader
      class="pageheader"
      :title="pageTitle"
      :description="pageDescription"
    />

    <UPageBody class="pagebody">
      <EntityIndexCta
        family="console"
        cta="Create or manage the entity."
      />

      <XCollectionManager />
    </UPageBody>
  </UPage>
</template>
```

## Page Owns
- route metadata
- page title and description
- one CTA/growth prompt
- which family collection manager is rendered
- app-level head/SEO only when the family requires it

## Collection Manager Owns
- fetching or consuming the canonical family collection seam
- pending and empty states
- search, filtering, variants, and display controls
- item links and item-level actions

## Hard No
- no `live | demo | test` source mode on public indexes
- no route aliases such as `.demo` or `.test`
- no dev-note blocks in public index pages
- no app-local plural barrels when the package/entity seam exists
- no second collection manager unless the family has a documented growth layer
- no duplicated title/description between header and CTA
- no parent page fetching when the collection manager is the canonical owner

## Accepted Deltas
- page copy
- nav metadata
- icon/order/layout visibility
- CTA wording
- collection manager component name
- app-specific visibility when documented in app config or Tier1 contract

## Stop Signal
If aligning one index needs a broad scattered diff, stop and identify the missing shared seam first.

Before editing an index family, name:
- family name
- reference sibling
- required matching seams
- allowed deltas
- files that should stay ignorant of the delta
